{
  "$comment": "#EXP-2124 (owner 2026-11-24) THE SIDEBAR MENUS, web md+ and the desktop IDE (PHONES, #EXP-2109: the same table as the long-press menu of the Teams tab's rows, minus `phone.drops`, `phoneCases`, sidebarPhoneMenu: a phone has no tabs; MOVE TO FOLDER's submenu = sidebarMoveTargets, `moveCases`). ONE menu table for every sidebar row, replayed by every client (the pure reference is `src/sidebar-menus.ts`, desktop Rust `domain::sidebar_menus`; each replays `menuCases`, `newCases`, `newTabCases` and compares the WHOLE expected value). A row's right-click (the keyboard's menu key; a long-press on touch) opens ITS kind's menu, drawn with THE genUI Menu (`openOn: contextmenu`); a row that also has a hover `…` (the team) opens the same menu from it. MENU (`kinds`, sidebarItemMenu(kind, input)): five GROUPS in the fixed order `groups` (open: Open, Open in new tab; kind: what only this kind does; arrange: Rename, Copy link, Move to folder, Add to / Remove from sidebar; settings; danger: destructive, last), a `separator` between the non-empty ones. An entry is an id, or {id, when}: shown only while the input flag `when` is true (`owner` = the viewer owns the item's team, `mine` = the viewer's own device, `canDelete` = chats.json `menuCases` delete rule). Labels are `copy` (a `danger` row is drawn destructive and asks first with the usual confirm); a verb that has a shortcut elsewhere shows it (`shortcuts`: New chat = the new session tab's Alt/Option+T); no other shortcut exists and none is invented here. The ONLY destructive row added is a board's Archive (owner; the board settings' archive behind its confirm); an Active row keeps the Delete it already had. VERBS: open = the row's own press; open-new-tab = the row's page as a NEW work tab opened in the BACKGROUND (the current tab stays; `tabs`): every kind that has Open is a tab now (Home, Needs you, Chats, Drafts, a device, a board, an app besides the issues, chats, agents and sessions tabs always held), a page already open as a tab is not opened twice; Home and the new session tab are ONE tab (key `new`, never two for Home): visiting Home opens or activates it, Open in new tab on Home adds it in the background, its chip is the Home nav icon + `Home`, the landing rule is unchanged (a chat started from its composer takes its place) and Alt/Option+T activates it; new-chat = Home's composer (the new session tab); new = THE New list as a submenu (`newKinds`); new-folder, rename (a folder: in place; a device: its name in place), ungroup = sidebar-folders.json; new-issue = the New issue page on that board; compact / new-conversation = chats.json `agentMenu.sends`; edit = the app editor; copy-link = the page's URL on the clipboard; move = a submenu of the team's folders (into that folder), then `New folder` (a new folder holding the item, its name in edit) and, for an item inside a folder, `Top level`; add-to-sidebar = sidebar-tree.json `drop` (appended to its team's list; hidden once placed); remove-from-sidebar = its entry deleted; settings = the item's settings page (the Assistant: Settings > Assistant; a device: its settings page; a team: the team settings; a board: its board settings; an app: the editor's Settings tab; an agent: its settings as the screen's opened item). THE NEW LIST (`newKinds`, sidebarNewKinds({owner})): ONE order everywhere a team creates something (the team menu's New, the new-tab menu's team submenu): Chat (every member; Home's composer with that team as its Teams pick), then Agent, App, Board (owners; settings-nav.json `newEntries`; their creation pages); labels `newCopy`. THE NEW-TAB MENU (`newTabCases`, newTabMenu): the tab strip's + opens a menu instead of a fixed tab: the Assistant first (its name + the brand mark; opens its chat; absent while the viewer has none), a separator, then one row per team in sidebar order (sidebar-tree.json `teams`), each a submenu of THE New list for that viewer. Alt/Option+T still opens the new session tab directly. THE ASSISTANT ROW: sidebar-tree.json `root` puts `assistant` first (the brand mark + the Assistant's name + its conversation's count badge; opens its chat); the FAB stays.",
